~ furnace_room
do freezePlayer()
*There is a furnace here. It hasn't been lit for a long time. Dust coats its interior.*
Queen: Let me show you something: how easily everything can slip away. See that button on the side of the furnace. Twist it high and step back quickly.

*show panel here*

<Character backs up automatically as flames burst from the furnace and catch the structure on fire>
do unfreezePlayer()
=> END

~ burn_spread
do freezePlayer()
<slow spread across the entire town and the burning of the thing blocking the exit>

Queen: Haunting, isn't it? Yet hard to look away.
Queen: Well, I suggest you do. The smoke will soon build despite the fire's age. The exit is now open for us to continue.
do unfreezePlayer()
=> END

~ get_bat
do freezePlayer()
*Its a dinky metal bat, it feels hollow. At the tip its covered in old blood.*
Queen:  If it was good enough for its last owner, its good enough for you.
*It may be a little big but its yours now. "Metal Bat" was added to your inventory.*
do playSound("res://resources/sfx/Common/Chequered Ink/map_open.wav")
do giveItem("Metal Bat")
do unfreezePlayer()
=> END